To make it sway with ocean currents and surround it with tiny bubbles, we can use CSS animations and some creative styling. Here's a possible implementation:

```css
.svg-container {
  position: relative;
  width: 32px;
  height: 32px;
  overflow: hidden;
}

.svg-container svg {
  position: absolute;
  top: 0;
  left: 0;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
}

.bubble-container {
  position: absolute;
  top: 0;
  left: 0;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  pointer-events: none;
}

.bubble {
  position: absolute;
  width: 2px;
  height: 2px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  background-color: #fff;
  animation: bubble-animation 2s infinite;
}

@keyframes bubble-animation {
  0% {
    transform: translate(0, 0);
  }
  50% {
    transform: translate(0, 5px);
  }
  100% {
    transform: translate(0, 0);
  }
}

.currents {
  position: absolute;
  top: 0;
  left: 0;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  pointer-events: none;
}

.current {
  position: absolute;
  width: 2px;
  height: 100%;
  background-color: #fff;
  animation: current-animation 2s infinite;
}

@keyframes current-animation {
  0% {
    transform: translate(0, 0);
  }
  50% {
    transform: translate(5px, 0);
  }
  100% {
    transform: translate(0, 0);
  }
}
```

