Next, let's create a CSS file (`style.css`) to style our parallax effect:
```css
.parallax-container {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100vh;
    overflow: hidden;
}

.parallax-svg {
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    left: 50%;
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
    z-index: 1;
}

.parallax-svg path {
    transition: transform 0.5s ease-in-out;
}

.parallax-container::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    background-image: linear-gradient(to bottom, #f92f60, #f92f60);
    background-size: 100% 0;
    background-position: 0 100%;
    transition: background-size 0.5s ease-in-out;
}

.parallax-container::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    background-image: linear-gradient(to bottom, #f92f60, #f92f60);
    background-size: 100% 0;
    background-position: 0 100%;
    transition: background-size 0.5s ease-in-out;
}

.parallax-container::before {
    z-index: 2;
}

.parallax-container::after {
    z-index: 3;
}

.parallax-container::before, .parallax-container::after {
    background-size: 100% 0;
    background-position: 0 100%;
}

.parallax-container::before {
    animation: parallax-effect 10s linear infinite;
}

.parallax-container::after {
    animation: parallax-effect 10s linear infinite;
    animation-delay: 5s;
}

@keyframes parallax-effect {
    0% {
